cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Gambling Harm Open Data"
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Five machine-readable datasets on gambling harm and gambling recovery in the
  United States, published together and refreshed on a stated clock. The set
  covers state-level gambling-harm publication and helpline contact volume for
  all 50 states and the District of Columbia; the responsible-gambling tools
  published by US sportsbook and daily-fantasy operators; a sourced glossary of
  gambling-recovery and gambling-industry terminology with stigma-preferred
  phrasing; a panel of quit-gambling apps listed on the US iOS App Store; and a
  directory of state and multi-state self-exclusion programs. Every value in
  every file carries the source it came from or an explicit marker saying why it
  does not. Produced by Betttr LLC, maker of a recovery app; no operator or
  affiliate money.
